---
title: Scones
yield: 12%scones
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
---

Preheat the oven to 220°C. Line a #baking tray{} with greaseproof paper.

Sift the @self-raising flour{225%g} and @salt{pinch} into a bowl. Using fingertips, lightly rub the @butter{55%g}(cold, cut into cubes) into the flour until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs. Add the @caster sugar{25%g} and the @milk{150%ml} and lightly mix until just combined. Avoid over mixing.

Tip the mixture out onto a lightly floured work surface. Using the palm of the hand, flatten out the dough out until it is about 2cm/1” thick (don't make too thin). Cut out 8-12 scones using a #58mm fluted cutter{}.

Place the scones on to the lined baking tray and bake for 11 to ~{13%minutes}, or until the scones are golden-brown and well-risen. Remove from the oven and place onto a wire rack until cool enough to handle.

Serve the scones with @clotted cream{} and either @./Sweet/Lemon Curd{} or @?strawberry jam{}.